From 864b18a944b79e5c398be85738db54d078362ce9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MasherDon <62326358+MasherDon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 04 Nov 2026 09:37:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 112/112] llama : SiegeLadder P19 stage B step 3 - the layer
 pool shrinks back to P11's 64 slots before the graph of the ubatch holding
 the C7 bound reaches the decoder layers, where the 512K scheduler buffer
 grows to 5438 MiB, plus a DXGI guard (LLAMA_DSV4_LAYER_MAJOR_POOL_GUARD_MIB,
 256); LLAMA_DSV4_LAYER_MAJOR_COST=2 times set_in per input class and carry_in
 per kind, sync no longer counts pull+copy's wait (L033); off by default; 48K
 equal byte for byte in exact and default at k 1 and 4 with the shrink firing
 in default; 512K k 1 -ub 2048 with the pool 457.96 tok/s against 390.30
 without, VRAM within budget (SiegeLadder runs.md 4.293)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
